---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../i18n/utils';
import { SITE, ADDRESS_FULL, COMPANY } from '../lib/constants';

const t = useTranslations();
const lastUpdated = 'August 1, 2026';
---

<PageLayout
  title={t('privacy.title')}
  description="Privacy policy for Sekoya.tech website. Learn how we handle your data."
  heroTitle={t('privacy.title')}
  heroDescription={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: t('privacy.title'), href: '/privacy-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="prose prose-invert prose-emerald max-w-none
    prose-headings:text-text prose-headings:font-bold
    prose-p:text-text-muted prose-p:leading-relaxed
    prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline
    prose-strong:text-text
    prose-li:text-text-muted
    prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:mb-4
    prose-h3:text-lg prose-h3:mt-8 prose-h3:mb-3">

    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      At {SITE.fullName} ("{SITE.name}"), we are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring transparency in how we handle your information. This Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, why we collect it, and how it is used when you visit our website at <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      We believe in minimal data collection. We set no cookies unless you explicitly consent to them, we do not track you across the web, and we do not sell or share your personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Collection</h2>

    <h3>Information You Provide</h3>
    <p>
      When you use our contact form, you voluntarily provide us with the following information:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Full name</strong> - so we can address you properly.</li>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> - so we can respond to your inquiry.</li>
      <li><strong>Subject and message</strong> - the content of your inquiry.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information is submitted through our contact form and processed by Web3Forms, a third-party form handling service, solely for the purpose of delivering your message to us. We do not store this information in any database on our servers.
    </p>

    <h3>Information We Do Not Collect</h3>
    <p>
      We do not collect, store, or process any of the following:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Payment or financial information</li>
      <li>Personally identifiable information beyond what you voluntarily submit</li>
      <li>Precise location data or device fingerprints</li>
      <li>Your browsing history on other websites</li>
      <li>Information from social media profiles</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our analytics providers do record which pages you view on this website, and infer an approximate location from your IP address. See <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a> below for exactly what each provider collects and which of them requires your consent.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and Consent</h2>
    <p>
      We set no cookies when you first arrive. On your first visit you will see a consent banner offering a clear choice between <strong>Accept</strong> and <strong>Reject</strong>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>If you reject</strong> (or simply ignore the banner), no cookies are set at any point and no Google Analytics code is ever loaded. The site remains fully functional.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>If you accept</strong>, we load Google Analytics 4, which sets its own first-party cookies (typically <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;id&gt;</code>) to distinguish visitors and measure sessions.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your choice itself is recorded in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> under the key <code>cookie-consent</code>, not in a cookie, and is never transmitted to our servers. Your theme preference (light/dark mode) is stored the same way.
    </p>

    <h3>Withdrawing or Changing Your Consent</h3>
    <p>
      You can change your mind at any time by clearing your browser's site data for this website — this removes the stored <code>cookie-consent</code> value along with any Google Analytics cookies, and the consent banner will appear again on your next visit. You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings, or opt out of Google Analytics entirely using Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>

    <h3>Plausible Analytics (no consent required)</h3>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://plausible.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible Analytics</a>, a privacy-focused, cookieless analytics service, on every visit. Plausible does not use cookies, does not collect personal data, and does not track visitors across websites. It complies with GDPR, CCPA, and PECR regulations without requiring consent, which is why it runs regardless of your choice in the banner.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plausible collects only aggregate, anonymized data such as:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Page views and referral sources</li>
      <li>Country of origin (inferred from anonymized IP, not stored)</li>
      <li>Browser and operating system type</li>
      <li>Device type (desktop, mobile, tablet)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No individual visitor profiles are created. All data is aggregated and cannot be used to identify any individual user. For more details, see the <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plausible Data Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Google Analytics 4 (consent required)</h3>
    <p>
      If — and only if — you accept cookies, we additionally load <a href="https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics 4</a> to understand how visitors use the site in more depth: which pages are read, how visitors navigate between them, and which content is most useful. Google Analytics processes data such as your IP address (truncated by Google), device and browser information, referral source, and the pages you view.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google acts as a data processor on our behalf and may process this data outside your country of residence. We do not use Google Analytics for advertising, remarketing, or audience sharing, and we do not link analytics data to any information you submit through our contact form. For details on how Google handles this data, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://business.safety.google/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy and terms for businesses</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

    <h3>Google Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      Loaded only after you accept cookies, as described under <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a> above. If you reject or ignore the consent banner, no request is ever made to Google.
    </p>

    <h3>Web3Forms</h3>
    <p>
      Our contact form submissions are processed by <a href="https://web3forms.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web3Forms</a>. When you submit the contact form, your name, email, and message are sent to Web3Forms, which then forwards them to our email inbox. Web3Forms does not sell or share your data. You can review their privacy policy on their website.
    </p>

    <h3>GitHub Pages</h3>
    <p>
      This website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may collect technical information such as IP addresses in server logs as part of their standard hosting operations. This data collection is governed by <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Since we do not operate a database or user account system, we do not retain personal data on our infrastructure. Contact form submissions are forwarded to our email and are retained only as long as necessary to respond to your inquiry and maintain business records.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request access to any personal data we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict the processing of your data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our website and services are not directed at individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last updated" date. We encourage you to review this page periodically.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Controller</h2>
    <p>
      The data controller responsible for the processing described in this policy is:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>{t('company.legal_name')}:</strong> {COMPANY.legalName}</li>
      <li><strong>{t('company.registered_office')}:</strong> {ADDRESS_FULL}</li>
      <li><strong>{t('company.tax_office')} / {t('company.tax_id')}:</strong> {COMPANY.taxOffice} / {COMPANY.taxId}</li>
      <li><strong>{t('company.mersis')}:</strong> {COMPANY.mersisNo}</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle your data, please contact us:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
      <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href={`tel:${SITE.phone.replace(/\s/g, '')}`}>{SITE.phone}</a></li>
      <li><strong>Address:</strong> {ADDRESS_FULL}</li>
      <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
